Love this upgrade 🔥 — a run history table makes your macro feel professional-grade.

Below is a clean, production-ready pattern:

Auto-clear current run

Log Start / End / Duration

Append each run to a History table

No overwriting, ever



---

📊 Suggested Layout

Summary Sheet

Cell	Purpose

A2	Start Date & Time
A3	End Date & Time
A4	Duration



---

History Sheet

Row 1 (Headers):

A	B	C	D

Run #	Start Date & Time	End Date & Time	Duration



---

1️⃣ Main Macro (Orchestrator)

Sub RunMainProcess()

    Call ClearTimeLog
    Call LogStartTime

    ' ===== YOUR MAIN PROCESS =====
    Application.Wait Now + TimeValue("00:00:05") ' sample workload
    ' =============================

    Call LogEndTimeAndDuration
    Call LogRunHistory

End Sub


---

2️⃣ Clear Current Run (Auto Reset)

Sub ClearTimeLog()

    With ThisWorkbook.Sheets("Summary")
        .Range("A2:A4").ClearContents
    End With

End Sub


---

3️⃣ Log Start Time

Sub LogStartTime()

    With ThisWorkbook.Sheets("Summary")
        .Range("A2").Value = Now
        .Range("A2").NumberFormat = "mm/dd/yyyy hh:mm:ss"
    End With

End Sub


---

4️⃣ Log End Time + Duration

Sub LogEndTimeAndDuration()

    Dim ws As Worksheet
    Dim startTime As Date
    Dim endTime As Date

    Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets("Summary")

    startTime = ws.Range("A2").Value
    endTime = Now

    ws.Range("A3").Value = endTime
    ws.Range("A3").NumberFormat = "mm/dd/yyyy hh:mm:ss"

    ws.Range("A4").Value = endTime - startTime
    ws.Range("A4").NumberFormat = "[hh]:mm:ss"

End Sub


---

5️⃣ ⭐ Append Run to History Table (Core Feature)

Sub LogRunHistory()

    Dim wsSum As Worksheet
    Dim wsHist As Worksheet
    Dim nextRow As Long
    Dim runNumber As Long

    Set wsSum = ThisWorkbook.Sheets("Summary")
    Set wsHist = ThisWorkbook.Sheets("History")

    ' Find next empty row
    nextRow = wsHist.Cells(wsHist.Rows.Count, "A").End(xlUp).Row + 1

    ' Auto run number
    If nextRow = 2 Then
        runNumber = 1
    Else
        runNumber = wsHist.Cells(nextRow - 1, "A").Value + 1
    End If

    wsHist.Cells(nextRow, "A").Value = runNumber
    wsHist.Cells(nextRow, "B").Value = wsSum.Range("A2").Value
    wsHist.Cells(nextRow, "C").Value = wsSum.Range("A3").Value
    wsHist.Cells(nextRow, "D").Value = wsSum.Range("A4").Value

    wsHist.Columns("B:C").NumberFormat = "mm/dd/yyyy hh:mm:ss"
    wsHist.Columns("D").NumberFormat = "[hh]:mm:ss"

End Sub


---

🧠 Why This Design Is Solid

✔ Each run is append-only
✔ No risk of overwriting previous logs
✔ Duration supports >24 hours
✔ Easy to export / audit / report
✔ Safe even if macro runs multiple times per day


